# schema — reserved, deliberately empty

This directory is empty on purpose, and this file exists only because git tracks
files rather than directories. It is not an unfinished source file.

What belongs here is the Zod validation layer: schemas describing the *active*
variant of a projection, and the `inactive-branches-not-validated` boundary that
keeps an invalid inactive branch from gating a valid document. Today that invariant
is proven at the store and in the browser suite; the schema module is where it gets
its own home once validation is more than the fixture needs.

Zod must not leak past this layer — `facade-owns-state` forbids product code from
importing it directly.

Governed by the `schema` route (docs/routes.json). The boundary rules that apply are
enforced, not described: `boundaries/element-types` in eslint.config.js and the
matching rules in .dependency-cruiser.cjs.

Delete this file once real source lands here.
